<template>
    <SiteShell page="features">
        <div class="page-head">
            <h1>Features</h1>
            <p class="lead">
                Three lines share one board document: layout, verification and
                fabrication handoff. Nothing here is assumed from a file
                extension, and the capability matrix is the only claim that
                counts.
            </p>
        </div>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Contracts</h2>
                <p>The shared contract every surface builds on.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="cards">
                <article class="contract">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
                    <h3>Handles</h3>
                    <p>
                        Creating or opening a board returns a handle. Every later
                        call names that handle, so the studio, CLI and SDK never
                        guess which document an operation belongs to.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="contract">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
                    <h3>Revisions</h3>
                    <p>
                        Every mutation increments the document revision and saves
                        store it. Concurrent-edit conflict handling is not
                        implemented yet; the revision is the anchor it will use.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="contract">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
                    <h3>Error codes</h3>
                    <p>
                        Errors are namespaced and stable. A call that cannot run keeps
                        <code>capability/not-implemented</code> instead of returning a
                        fabricated success.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="contract">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
                    <h3>Capability matrix</h3>
                    <p>
                        Board engine, project operations, formats, checks,
                        renderers and export targets each report their own status.
                        Unsupported is a first-class answer.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Layout</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li>Copper layers, stackup, footprints, nets, tracks and vias live in one board.</li>
                <li>A new board starts with F.Cu, B.Cu, front and back silkscreen; a rectangular outline is optional and checked by DRC.</li>
                <li>Layers can be added, renamed, hidden and locked; a rename rewrites footprint and track references in the same edit.</li>
                <li>Each handle keeps the last 32 snapshots; undo and redo restore them and commit a new revision.</li>
                <li>Every mutation increments the document revision; saves write a temporary file and rename it into place.</li>
                <li>Footprints move and update, tracks and vias delete in place, and lock rules block writes to a locked layer.</li>
                <li>Rejecting duplicate references or undeclared nets keeps one coherent document.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Verification</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li>Checks are named, not implied: DRC, connectivity, clearance, annular rings, stackup, outline and netlist run today.</li>
                <li>Every finding carries its rule code, revision, layer and object where the rule can name one.</li>
                <li>A missing or zero-size outline is an error; footprints, tracks and vias outside it are warnings.</li>
                <li>A board with an outline and no violations passes; errors fail with the objects involved.</li>
                <li>Silkscreen and courtyard are declared unsupported and report a warning instead of passing.</li>
                <li>Review is textual today: the interactive viewport renderer is not implemented.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Fabrication</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--warn">partial</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li>Gerber RS-274X, drill (Excellon), bill of materials, pick-and-place and SVG are written from the open revision.</li>
                <li>Gerber writes F_Cu, B_Cu, F_SilkS and Edge_Cuts files into a directory; the outline supplies the edge cuts.</li>
                <li>STEP, IPC-2581, KiCad and PDF are declared but not implemented.</li>
                <li>An export reports its format, revision, path, byte count and, for Gerber, every artifact name and size.</li>
                <li>Unsupported targets reject with <code>capability/not-implemented</code>; writers use board coordinates, never hand-written geometry.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Assembly</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--ok">available</span>
            </div>
            <ul>
                <li>Position files carry designator, value, package, mid X, mid Y, rotation and side.</li>
                <li>The bill of materials groups parts by value and footprint with quantity and designators.</li>
                <li>Both are derived from the same revision the inspection saw.</li>
                <li>STEP and IPC-2581 remain declared exchange targets without a writer.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Command surface</h2>
                <p>What each entry point actually does today.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Surface</th>
                            <th>What exists today</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="cell-mono">CLI</td>
                            <td>
                                <code>create</code>, <code>list</code>, <code>inspect</code>,
                                <code>undo</code>, <code>redo</code> and
                                <code>export gbr|drl|bom|pos|svg</code> run. Footprint add, move, update
                                and delete, track add and delete, via add and delete, net add,
                                <code>layer add|rename|visible|lock</code> and <code>outline set</code>
                                edit a document in place. STEP, IPC-2581, KiCad and PDF exports reject.
                            </td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--ok">available</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="cell-mono">SDK</td>
                            <td>
                                <code>@wae/open-pcb</code> exposes create, open, inspect, save,
                                export, undo, redo, addFootprint, moveFootprint, updateFootprint,
                                deleteFootprint, addTrack, deleteTrack, addVia, deleteVia, addNet,
                                addLayer, updateLayer, setOutline, list and close on one handle.
                            </td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--ok">available</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="cell-mono">Studio</td>
                            <td>
                                The VMZ shell talks to the host over JSON-RPC and shows board
                                facts, outline, undo and redo, layer visibility and lock toggles,
                                an add-layer form, export target status, supported checks,
                                inspection results and diagnostics. The canvas renderer and
                                viewport tools are not implemented.
                            </td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--warn">shell only</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="cell-mono">Skills</td>
                            <td>
                                <code>@wae/open-pcb-skills</code> carries executable commands,
                                preflight and safety rules for create, edit, undo/redo, layers,
                                outline and the five implemented exports.
                            </td>
                            <td><span class="chip chip--ok">available</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Format honesty</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--idle">10 declared</span>
            </div>
            <p>
                The format registry classifies KiCad board, Gerber, drill,
                position, bill of materials, STEP, IPC-2581, SVG, PDF and PNG
                files. Classification is not a support claim: an extension may be
                listed while the capability matrix still reports it as
                <code>unsupported</code>.
            </p>
            <p class="formats-cell cell-mono">
                kicad_pcb · gbr · drl · pos · bom · step · ipc2581 · svg · pdf · png
            </p>
            <p>
                Export is implemented for gbr, drl, bom, pos and svg. Checks run for drc,
                connectivity, clearance, annular_rings, stackup, outline and netlist;
                silkscreen and courtyard stay unsupported. Renderers are declared as svg,
                png and pdf, and only svg has a writer.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Current state</h2>
                <span class="chip chip--idle">no public release</span>
            </div>
            <p>
                The document core, undo and redo, layer management, the outline,
                in-place CLI editing, rule checks and five output writers are
                implemented and covered by Rust and TypeScript tests. The interactive
                renderer, STEP, IPC-2581, KiCad import/export and PDF remain ahead.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-band">
